[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own table says
otherwise. The queued parser fix closes only `parser`.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue: two causes, one ticket each. Fixing the parser leaves `hint` open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Each row is a cause, and each cause has its own ticket:

- **`parser`** — [ticket #1](https://github.com/kjoetftfke/mega-s01e03/issues/1). The shared
  parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and month swapped: 7 April
  becomes 4 July.
- **`hint`** — [ticket #2](https://github.com/kjoetftfke/mega-s01e03/issues/2). The table marks it
  "no ticket of its own"; now it has one. booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.
  People at a day-first tenant type month first, as told, and the form reads it day first. Same
  symptom, different code: the parser fix does not reach it.

## How the reports were placed

The table above is the desk's own view: each report counted once by id (the export pages
overlap, so some rows repeat), filed under its cause by tenant and the way it came in (`causeOf`
in `causes.ts`).
The reports in the footnote belong to `parser`: `causeOf` ties them there by tenant, so they are
counted in ticket #1 and nowhere else.

Intake's tag is no guide here: it guesses from the reporter's browser, not the tenant, so it
tags `hint` reports `parser` and `parser` reports `hint`. The table counts by tenant.

## For the desk

- Close each cause on its own ticket. #4471 stays open until both are fixed.
- Merging on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put them all under
  one ticket: "Date is wrong" and "Month and day swapped?" come in under both causes.

